.TH AENIGMA-KEYS 8 "2026-08-12" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-keys \- generate an RSA key pair for the Aenigma service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-keys
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-keys
generates a new RSA private/public key pair for the Aenigma service
using
.BR openssl (1).
It takes no options or arguments.
.PP
The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Creates the directory
.I /var/lib/aenigma
if it does not already exist.
.IP \(bu 2
Generates a
.B 4096
bit RSA private key, encrypted with
.B AES-256
under a passphrase, and writes it to
.IR /var/lib/aenigma/private\-key.pem .
Because the private key is encrypted,
.BR openssl (1)
interactively prompts for a passphrase (and confirmation) on the
controlling terminal; this step cannot be run fully unattended
without additional input redirection.
.IP \(bu 2
Derives the corresponding public key from the private key and
writes it, unencrypted, to
.IR /var/lib/aenigma/public\-key.pem .
.IP \(bu 2
Sets ownership of both files to
.B aenigma:aenigma
and permissions to
.BR 700 ,
restricting read access to the
.B aenigma
user only.
.PP
.B aenigma-keys
must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.B aenigma-keys
takes no command-line options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The key pair was generated and stored successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The script was not run as root, or
.BR openssl (1)
failed (for example, if the passphrase prompt was aborted).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/aenigma/private\-key.pem
The generated RSA private key, AES-256 encrypted under a
user-supplied passphrase. Owned by
.B aenigma:aenigma
with mode
.BR 700 .
.TP
.I /var/lib/aenigma/public\-key.pem
The corresponding RSA public key, unencrypted. Owned by
.B aenigma:aenigma
with mode
.BR 700 .
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a new key pair, entering a passphrase when prompted:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-keys
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
.B aenigma-keys
does not check whether a key pair already exists before running.
Re-running it
.B overwrites
.I private\-key.pem
and
.I public\-key.pem
unconditionally with a newly generated pair and a new passphrase,
with no backup and no confirmation prompt. Any data encrypted, or
peers trusting, the previous key pair will no longer validate
against the new one. Back up the existing key files before
re-running this script if the previous key pair must be preserved.
.PP
Mode
.B 700
on
.I public\-key.pem
means only the
.B aenigma
user can read the public key, even though public keys are not
normally treated as secret; if another user or service needs to
read the public key directly from disk, its permissions will need
to be relaxed separately.
.PP
Because the private key is passphrase-protected, any service or
process that loads it at startup must be supplied with that
passphrase through some out-of-band mechanism (interactive prompt,
environment variable, secrets manager, etc.); this script does not
address key loading, only generation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openssl (1),
.BR aenigma-config (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>
